// FlowTransitionResult — the outcome of Graph.executeFlowTransition() (Graph
// Flows spec §11.3). `success` true carries the §6.2 step 8 `newState` the
// instance advanced to. On a rejection `success` is false and `reason` explains
// it; `guardDescription` is the §7 transition's human-readable guard gloss (set
// when the §7 guard did not hold); `secondsUntilAllowed` is the remaining §8
// minDelay wait as a decimal string (set only on a minDelay rejection).

dictionary FlowTransitionResult {
  required boolean success;
  DOMString? newState;
  USVString? reason;
  USVString? guardDescription;
  DOMString? secondsUntilAllowed;
};
